bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    wm_local_lane_clock_tick_full_repaint_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-26 wm-lane-20261126 Linux aarch64 seed fb80903917d6d5f5: red = wm_retained_damage_behavior_spec 6/8 (clock-rect plan examples missing). Fix records the taskbar-clock text box (engine2d_wm_clock_rect, 2px AA pad) per presented frame and marks old+new boxes instead of returning FULL; unknown box still fails closed. Green: behavior 8/8, engine2d_wm_local_lane_clock_tick_spec 2/2 (fluid_light + aetheric_dark, 160x120, replayed frame == fresh CPU executor frame, outside box == previous device frame, glyphs changed) on NVIDIA GB10 and llvmpipe. Perf GB10 tick 305-325ms -> 134-157ms over 3 alternated rounds; first frame unchanged."
    wm_local_lane_clock_tick_full_repaint_2026-11-26, 1, "2026-11-26 Fable review FIX-FIRST: the LOCAL clock path is unreachable in production because simpleos_runtime_taskbar_revision mixes the clock text into taskbar_revision; same-revision LOCAL plans also miss lane-switch, late-content and theme-generation invalidation; clip proof compared the mirror to itself and the window was degraded (no content frame). Status reverted until fixed."
    wm_local_lane_clock_tick_full_repaint_2026-11-26, 2, "2026-11-26 seed fb80903917d6d5f5 FIX-FIRST items addressed: clock-independent taskbar layout key in the executor (taskbar_revision kept clock-dependent: shell need_render gate, input, rv64/arm64 producers and ssh entry use it as repaint trigger); frame key folds lane/theme/palette/degraded/content; host-gpu present invalidates. wm_retained_clock_tick_spec 5/5 (red on pre-fix: example 1 expected software-retained-damage); local-lane clock tick device spec 2/2 GB10 + llvmpipe with fresh full device readback + canary, window under clock. Perf 3 alternated rounds vs 16caf04da27: window-misses-clock tick 5.42-5.48 s -> 52-54 ms; window-under-clock tick 5.72-5.78 s -> 5.68-5.72 s (no win, no regression). Earlier 134-157 ms figure withdrawn. Awaiting re-review."
    wm_local_lane_clock_tick_full_repaint_2026-11-26, 3, "2026-11-27 Fable re-review (item-1 deviation judged sound) BLOCKING fix: frame key pins resolved window ids, not content URIs; a changed content URI damages only that window's full bounds (unknown id -> FULL); layout-key fields percent-escape %, |, ;. wm_retained_clock_tick_spec 8/8 through render() (content update and move both take software-retained-damage and equal a fresh executor frame); red on ee1c5b9100c: those two plus the escape example fail (path stays software). Device clock spec 3/3 on NVIDIA GB10 + llvmpipe incl. restored aetheric_dark (fails closed to FULL, parent-sampling). Perf: any replay touching a window costs about a full frame on Vulkan."
